title: "GQ: Merging and retrofitting data and models"
type: software
version: "1.0.1"
license: LGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/cascadiaquakes/gq"
authors:
  - family-names: Ajala
    given-names: Rasheed
    affiliation: "Lamont-Doherty Earth Observatory, Columbia University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5650-8362"
  - name: "CRESCENT cyberinfrastructure team"
    website: "https://cascadiaquakes.org/"
abstract: "GQ (GridQuery) is a collection of command-line programs for merging multiscale and multiresolution data and models, and retrofitting three-dimensional Earth models by adding shallow geotechnical layering, modifying their topography and bathymetry, and generating or applying statistically defined small-scale heterogeneities. GQ builds on BLEND and the Generic Mapping Tools (GMT)."
